# tools/glyph_compose_witness.rish -- the combining-diacritic overlay proves itself on metal (Season G, the accent primitive).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) - the primitive that collapses the accent grind. The long run of hand-drawn accent
# corpora (grave, acute, circumflex, tilde, diaeresis over the same 5x7 body) taught a discovery: an accented Latin
# letter is a BASE letter plus a COMBINING mark, and the mark lives entirely in the two blank rows above the letter.
# image/glyph_compose.rye adds one bounded verb -- overlay(base, mark, cell_area) -- an ink union over the coverage grid
# every glyph already carries, and proves the discovery on metal: overlay(lowercase 'a', grave mark) equals the
# hand-drawn 'a grave' coverage BYTE-FOR-BYTE, and the same for e, o, u, so the grind was composition all along. The
# verb is commutative, a blank mark is the identity, and a wrong-length input or a bad cell area refuses by name. This
# retires O(letters x accents) hand-drawing to O(letters + accents) composition. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/glyph_compose_witness.rish

say "glyph-compose: Language EN -- Season G open-media primitive; a combining-diacritic overlay over the 5x7 coverage grid, proving overlay(base,mark) reproduces the hand-drawn grave vowels byte-for-byte so every accented letter is composition, not a fresh drawing."
say "glyph-compose: Style Radiant -- the corpora that already shipped are the specification; overlay(lowercase 'a', grave mark) equals the hand-drawn 'a grave' byte-for-byte, so the primitive reproduces what the grind drew by hand, our own open font, no external font to license."
say "glyph-compose: Lens TAME -- u32 in-memory counts, u8 coverage bytes; cell_area bounded by the atlas ceiling; each function states its invariants positively (the union is a superset of both inputs, adds no ink beyond their sum); refusals named (BadCellArea - BaseLenMismatch - MarkLenMismatch); no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/glyph_compose"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/glyph_compose.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "glyph-compose: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "glyph-compose: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "glyph-compose: ${out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1 | grep -q 'GREEN image-glyph-compose' && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "glyph-compose: selftest did not print the GREEN primitive line"
